      <div class="member__bio">
        <p class="member__lead">Francis Agbotse is a compassionate Psychiatric Mental Health Nurse Practitioner who brings a unique blend of medical education, psychiatric expertise, and genuine curiosity about the human experience to his work at Meaningful Psychiatry.</p>
        <p>With over a decade of experience in psychiatry, Francis is passionate about helping patients move toward meaningful, lasting change—whether that means finding relief from symptoms, strengthening relationships, improving daily functioning, or reconnecting with a sense of purpose.</p>

        <h3>Education &amp; Training</h3>
        <p>Francis is an <strong>International Medical Graduate (IMG)</strong> who completed medical education at <strong>Windsor School of Medicine in Saint Kitts</strong> before pursuing advanced psychiatric-mental health nursing education at the <strong>University of Alabama at Birmingham</strong>. This combination of medical and psychiatric training gives him a broad clinical perspective and a strong foundation for caring for patients with a wide range of mental health concerns.</p>

        <h3>Clinical Focus</h3>
        <p>He is particularly well equipped to work with <strong>complex psychiatric presentations, multiple diagnoses, and complicated medication regimens</strong>. His clinical experience includes comprehensive psychiatric evaluations, diagnostic assessment, and evidence-based psychopharmacology, allowing him to thoughtfully consider both the complexity of a patient’s symptoms and the larger context of their health.</p>

        <h3>Approach to Care</h3>
        <p>At the heart of Francis’s practice is the belief that meaningful care begins with feeling <strong>heard, respected, and understood</strong>. He takes time to learn each patient’s unique history, strengths, values, goals, cultural background, and lived experiences. His approach is collaborative and patient-centered, creating space for patients to actively participate in decisions about their care.</p>
        <p>Depending on each patient’s needs, Francis may incorporate <strong>medication management, psychotherapy, lifestyle and behavioral strategies, and collaboration with other members of the care team</strong>. He strives to provide care that is compassionate, affirming, conscientious, and grounded in evidence-based medicine.</p>

        <div class="callout">
          <h3>Insurance &amp; Availability</h3>
          <p>Francis is <strong>currently accepting Aetna, Ambetter, and Coordinated Care (Medicare + Medicaid).</strong> He is working to expand his in-network availability with additional insurance plans. We are building a waitlist for patients with the following plans:</p>
          <ul class="chips chips--plain">
            <li>Cigna</li><li>Optum Behavioral Health</li><li>Premera Blue Cross</li><li>Regence BlueShield</li><li>TriWest</li><li>First Choice Health</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Additional insurance coverage will be available as credentialing expands.</p>
        </div>

        <p class="member__closing">Francis is excited to be part of the Meaningful Psychiatry team and to walk alongside patients as they work toward greater stability, understanding, and well-being.</p>
      </div>
