        <p class="member__lead">Sanaa Syed is our dedicated coordinator at Meaningful Psychiatry! She is on her way to becoming an MD herself, and a future budding psychiatrist, and we are so happy to have her here as your first point of contact at Meaningful Psychiatry!</p>

        <h3>How Sanaa Helps</h3>
        <p>She coordinates patient care with thoughtfulness and intentionality, managing intake and scheduling, guiding patients through the administrative journey, ensuring seamless communication between patients and provider, and creating an environment where every individual feels welcomed and heard.</p>

        <h3>Background</h3>
        <p>Sanaa currently holds a B.S. in Informatics (Biomedical &amp; Health Systems) and a minor in Bioethics from the University of Washington Seattle. Because of her academic background and experience, Sanaa brings a holistic understanding of medicine, where data, ethics, and humanity intersect.</p>
        <p>Sanaa’s diverse clinical foundation spans pediatric research at Seattle Children’s Research Institute, patient services and care coordination at Kaiser Permanente, behavioral health therapy with children and families at Kids and Family Counseling, and clinical project coordination at UW Medicine. Her research on post-kidney transplant care was published in the Journal of the American Medical Informatics Association in 2024.</p>

        <p class="member__closing">We are so excited to have Sanaa onboard as part of our team here at Meaningful Psychiatry. Welcome aboard Sanaa!</p>
